How can I check if a string contains only numeric characters in C#?
Input code: 
string str = "12345";
Data format:
You must have [C# code] data type in the following Rewrite prompt
Solution:
In C#, you can use the int.TryParse method to check if a string contains only numeric characters. Here's an example:
string str = "12345";
int result;
bool isNumeric = int.TryParse(str, out result);
If the string contains only numeric characters, the isNumeric variable will be set to true, and the value of result will be the parsed integer. If the string contains non-numeric characters, isNumeric will be set to false, and the value of result will be 0.
Alternatively, you can use regular expressions to check if a string contains only numeric characters. Here's an example:
string str = "12345";
bool isNumeric = System.Text.RegularExpressions.Regex.IsMatch(str, @"^\d+$");
This will return true if the string contains only numeric characters, and false otherwise.

